For Histogram visualization, describe and justify: 
    > What software did you use to create your data visualization? 
    Microsoft Excel

    > Who is your intended audience? 
    Government agencies and policymakers interested in funding distribution.
    
    > What information or message are you trying to convey with your visualization? 
    I am trying to show how grant amounts are distributed across different ranges to identify common funding levels and potential gaps. 
    I am also trying to show where most funding is concentrated (mode), the spread of funding values (range, skewness) and potential outliers (very high or low grants), which can inform funding strategies.

    > What aspects of design did you consider when making your visualization? How did you apply them? With what elements of your plots? 
    I choose a bin width size of $16,000 to balance detail and readability
    I used blue green color for the bars on a white background to make the plot visually appealing and easy to read.
    I used clear labels (Grant Amount on x-axis, Frequency on y-axis) and a descriptive title (Distribution of grant amounts) to ensure the audience understands the plot easily.


    > How did you ensure that your data visualizations are reproducible? If the tool you used to make your data visualization is not reproducible, how will this impact your data visualization? 
   Excel is not inherently reproducible like coding environments (e.g., Python and R) but I documented the steps taken to create the histogram, including bin width selection, design choices and axis labeling.

    > How did you ensure that your data visualization is accessible?  
     I used a clear and high-contrast colors (dark blue bars on white background)
     I used readable  and bold font sizes for labels and title
     I added axis labels and a title to provide context
     I ensured bins are interpretable for numeric literacy differences

    > Who are the individuals and communities who might be impacted by your visualization?  
    Government agencies, policymakers, and settlement service organizations in Ontario who allocate and receive funding for newcomer settlement programs.

    > How did you choose which features of your chosen dataset to include or exclude from your visualization? 
    I focused on the "Grant Amount" feature as it directly relates to funding distribution, which is the main message I want to convey.

    > What ‘underwater labour’ contributed to your final data visualization product?
    
    Data exploration: I analyzed the distribution of grant amounts to determine appropriate bin widths and ranges for the histogram.
    Design iteration: I experimented with different color schemes, bin sizes, and labeling to enhance clarity and visual appeal.     